        "sha": "83ea0b9ad820f1af90eb3951d31452a2067824f8",
        "message": "os/: Add crash diagnostic capture driver (/dev/crashrpt)\n\nAdd crashrpt driver that enables user-space reporters to capture\ndiagnostic data during system crashes. The driver registers a callback\nat the top of up_assert() that wakes a registered reporter thread\nbefore crash handling begins.\n\nFeatures:\n- Reporter thread registers via ioctl and parks in fin_wait()\n- Kernel wakes reporter with crash reason when assert occurs\n- Reporter writes diagnostic data to file using kernel file APIs\n- Atomic file operations (temp file + rename) prevent partial writes\n- Configurable deadline (default 3000ms) for report completion"
      },
      {
        "sha": "2376ac39edd73b8bbc67340c240e94f76e4e7b31",
        "message": "os/drivers/dev_null.c: Add ioctl handler to trigger kernel assert for testing\n\nAdd an ioctl handler to the /dev/null driver that triggers a kernel assert when called with a non-NULL argument. This is intended for testing the crash report capture mechanism."
      }
    ],
